# No Scene or Asset Edits

**NEVER modify Unity scene files, prefabs, or other serialized editor assets unless the user explicitly asks you to in that message.**

This includes:
- `Assets/**/*.unity` (scenes)
- `Assets/**/*.prefab` (prefabs)
- `ProjectSettings/**`
- Any YAML/serialized Unity asset (materials, animators, ScriptableObjects, etc.)
- Static flags, layer assignments, transform values, component references, or hierarchy in those files

**Allowed without explicit request:** C# scripts in `Assets/Scripts/` (and other code files) when the task requires code changes.

**If a task needs scene/prefab setup:** tell the user exactly what to set in the Unity Editor — do not edit the asset files yourself.

**If unsure:** ask first. Do not touch scenes "to help" or "to test."
